---
// Herzberg: satisfaction and dissatisfaction run on two separate scales.
---
<div class="hz">
  <div class="hz-row">
    <div class="hz-head"><b>Motivators</b><span>Achievement · recognition · responsibility · advancement · growth</span></div>
    <div class="hz-scale"><span class="hz-l">No satisfaction</span><i class="hz-bar ok"></i><span class="hz-r">Satisfaction</span></div>
    <p>Enrich the work itself to move people right.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="hz-row">
    <div class="hz-head"><b>Hygiene factors</b><span>Pay · policy · supervision · working conditions · job security</span></div>
    <div class="hz-scale"><span class="hz-l">Dissatisfaction</span><i class="hz-bar warn"></i><span class="hz-r">No dissatisfaction</span></div>
    <p>Fixing these only gets you to neutral: no complaints, no extra drive.</p>
  </div>
</div>
